            <ArticleTitle>Geriatric Infectious Diseases: Current Concepts on Diagnosis and Management.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>631-641</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1111/jgs.14731</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>New information on infectious diseases in older adults has become available in the past 20 years. In this review, in-depth discussions on the general problem of geriatric infectious diseases (epidemiology, pathogenesis, age-related host defenses, clinical manifestations, diagnostic approach); diagnosis and management of bacterial pneumonia, urinary tract infection, and Clostridium difficile infection; and the unique challenges of diagnosing and managing infections in a long-term care setting are presented.</AbstractText>
